(4335322, 623493, 49109, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your top10 finish and new PB. Very well done!</td>', 'Congrats on your top10 finish and new PB. Very well done!', '2007-12-26 04:30:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4335335, 623044, 40973, '<td valign="top">The photograph is about the yellow ribbon.</td>', 'The photograph is about the yellow ribbon.', '2007-12-26 04:47:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4335346, 622790, 19708, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by robst:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice shot, how can anyone give this a 3 or even a 4? <br/> </i></td></tr></table> <br/>It''s a very good shot, but in my eyes doesn''t meet the challenge. That''s how. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I generally don''t openly disagree with members, but this deserves my 2 cents.<br/>Landscapes are pretty, a lot of what is around us is pretty, beautiful even, but to see an elderly couple, walking together such as this, to me, is one of the most precious and beautiful things our lives can wish for. The landscapes and pretty things around us will still be there in 20, 50, 100 years, but the moments as seen in this great example of the bond of two human beings, will last but moments, and we all should take the time to see this as one of the great goals while we live on this planet.<br/> <br/>Thank you for this shot Adrian, and congrats on your Blue Ribbon.</td>', 'Originally posted by eyewave: Originally posted by robst: Nice shot, how can anyone give this a 3 or even a 4?   It''s a very good shot, but in my eyes doesn''t meet the challenge. That''s how.  I generally don''t openly disagree with members, but this deserves my 2 cents.Landscapes are pretty, a lot of what is around us is pretty, beautiful even, but to see an elderly couple, walking together such as this, to me, is one of the most precious and beautiful things our lives can wish for. The landscapes and pretty things around us will still be there in 20, 50, 100 years, but the moments as seen in this great example of the bond of two human beings, will last but moments, and we all should take the time to see this as one of the great goals while we live on this planet. Thank you for this shot Adrian, and congrats on your Blue Ribbon.', '2007-12-26 05:00:36.000000', NULL, 0),
