(4337464, 622790, 11518, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Brad:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by robst:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice shot, how can anyone give this a 3 or even a 4? <br/> </i></td></tr></table> <br/>It''s a very good shot, but in my eyes doesn''t meet the challenge. That''s how. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I generally don''t openly disagree with members, but this deserves my 2 cents.<br/>Landscapes are pretty, a lot of what is around us is pretty, beautiful even, but to see an elderly couple, walking together such as this, to me, is one of the most precious and beautiful things our lives can wish for. The landscapes and pretty things around us will still be there in 20, 50, 100 years, but the moments as seen in this great example of the bond of two human beings, will last but moments, and we all should take the time to see this as one of the great goals while we live on this planet.<br/> <br/>Thank you for this shot Adrian, and congrats on your Blue Ribbon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree 100% with you Brad!<br/> <br/>And Congrats on a well deserved Blue Adrian.</td>', 'Originally posted by Brad: Originally posted by eyewave: Originally posted by robst: Nice shot, how can anyone give this a 3 or even a 4?   It''s a very good shot, but in my eyes doesn''t meet the challenge. That''s how.  I generally don''t openly disagree with members, but this deserves my 2 cents.Landscapes are pretty, a lot of what is around us is pretty, beautiful even, but to see an elderly couple, walking together such as this, to me, is one of the most precious and beautiful things our lives can wish for. The landscapes and pretty things around us will still be there in 20, 50, 100 years, but the moments as seen in this great example of the bond of two human beings, will last but moments, and we all should take the time to see this as one of the great goals while we live on this planet. Thank you for this shot Adrian, and congrats on your Blue Ribbon.   I agree 100% with you Brad! And Congrats on a well deserved Blue Adrian.', '2007-12-26 23:30:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4337901, 622790, 66616, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by doctornick:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Brad:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by robst:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice shot, how can anyone give this a 3 or even a 4? <br/> </i></td></tr></table> <br/>It''s a very good shot, but in my eyes doesn''t meet the challenge. That''s how. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I generally don''t openly disagree with members, but this deserves my 2 cents.<br/>Landscapes are pretty, a lot of what is around us is pretty, beautiful even, but to see an elderly couple, walking together such as this, to me, is one of the most precious and beautiful things our lives can wish for. The landscapes and pretty things around us will still be there in 20, 50, 100 years, but the moments as seen in this great example of the bond of two human beings, will last but moments, and we all should take the time to see this as one of the great goals while we live on this planet.<br/> <br/>Thank you for this shot Adrian, and congrats on your Blue Ribbon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree 100% with you Brad!<br/> <br/>And Congrats on a well deserved Blue Adrian. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>How can this image not meet the challenge? Beauty in the everyday!I see old couples walking around holding hands everyday and this image is especially beautiful. It obviously has met the challenge in the eyes of many of the voters.</td>', 'Originally posted by doctornick: Originally posted by Brad: Originally posted by eyewave: Originally posted by robst: Nice shot, how can anyone give this a 3 or even a 4?   It''s a very good shot, but in my eyes doesn''t meet the challenge. That''s how.  I generally don''t openly disagree with members, but this deserves my 2 cents.Landscapes are pretty, a lot of what is around us is pretty, beautiful even, but to see an elderly couple, walking together such as this, to me, is one of the most precious and beautiful things our lives can wish for. The landscapes and pretty things around us will still be there in 20, 50, 100 years, but the moments as seen in this great example of the bond of two human beings, will last but moments, and we all should take the time to see this as one of the great goals while we live on this planet. Thank you for this shot Adrian, and congrats on your Blue Ribbon.   I agree 100% with you Brad! And Congrats on a well deserved Blue Adrian.   How can this image not meet the challenge? Beauty in the everyday!I see old couples walking around holding hands everyday and this image is especially beautiful. It obviously has met the challenge in the eyes of many of the voters.', '2007-12-27 05:19:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4337978, 623227, 61679, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for kind words and the votes.  It figures, the one time I forget to put my processing steps in the comment section and I ribbon.  Here are the steps I used.<br/> <br/>1. Convert from raw using Raw Shooters Essentials<br/>Exposure Comp [+1.23]<br/>Highlight Contrast [22]<br/> <br/>2. Post process with Paint Shop Pro X<br/>One step noise reduction<br/>Clarify [+20]<br/>USM [radius 50 - strength 15 - clip 3]<br/>USM [radius 0.3 - strength 300 - clip 3]<br/>Levels [input 0-.94-255 / output 0-241]<br/>Curve - slight S curve to set black point<br/>Resize<br/>USM [radius 50 - strength 15 - clip 3]<br/>USM [radius 0.3 - strength 300 - clip 3]<br/> <br/>The HDR effect came from the very strong clarify action.  On most images, using clarify over a strength of 7 or 8 will provide nasty over processing artifacts.  The max setting of 20 seemed to work well for this image.<br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'Thanks everyone for kind words and the votes.  It figures, the one time I forget to put my processing steps in the comment section and I ribbon.  Here are the steps I used. 1. Convert from raw using Raw Shooters EssentialsExposure Comp [+1.23]Highlight Contrast [22] 2. Post process with Paint Shop Pro XOne step noise reductionClarify [+20]USM [radius 50 - strength 15 - clip 3]USM [radius 0.3 - strength 300 - clip 3]Levels [input 0-.94-255 / output 0-241]Curve - slight S curve to set black pointResizeUSM [radius 50 - strength 15 - clip 3]USM [radius 0.3 - strength 300 - clip 3] The HDR effect came from the very strong clarify action.  On most images, using clarify over a strength of 7 or 8 will provide nasty over processing artifacts.  The max setting of 20 seemed to work well for this image. Tim', '2007-12-27 06:46:56.000000', NULL, 0),
