(4342092, 622790, 69246, '<td valign="top">I''m sorry to hear about the DQ...it was truely an amazing shot.</td>', 'I''m sorry to hear about the DQ...it was truely an amazing shot.', '2007-12-28 21:39:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342130, 622790, 68972, '<td valign="top">This is a very moving image.  Keep up the great work and thanks for sharing!</td>', 'This is a very moving image.  Keep up the great work and thanks for sharing!', '2007-12-28 22:08:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342202, 623851, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot.  The tension between the fresh berries and the dying berries is wonderful.  In fact, I would''ve cropped it so the blue ones are closer to the bottom and the red ones are closer to the right edge to make that contrast even stronger.  Yes, it''s a multi-subject composition - that''s the point. :)</td>', 'I like this a lot.  The tension between the fresh berries and the dying berries is wonderful.  In fact, I would''ve cropped it so the blue ones are closer to the bottom and the red ones are closer to the right edge to make that contrast even stronger.  Yes, it''s a multi-subject composition - that''s the point. :)', '2007-12-28 23:26:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342203, 623227, 81784, '<td valign="top">i like this, so nice. look so good!!</td>', 'i like this, so nice. look so good!!', '2007-12-28 23:27:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342204, 623671, 81784, '<td valign="top">WOW.. nice still life photography..<br/>i love this pic.</td>', 'WOW.. nice still life photography..i love this pic.', '2007-12-28 23:27:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342361, 622790, 80878, '<td valign="top">cool shot! yeah i would have done the same. about them saying no... thats just a formality... lol yu dont ven need toask, especialy for these shots! (as long as they are in public.)</td>', 'cool shot! yeah i would have done the same. about them saying no... thats just a formality... lol yu dont ven need toask, especialy for these shots! (as long as they are in public.)', '2007-12-29 01:35:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342381, 623671, 42013, '<td valign="top">Well done as always. Congrats!</td>', 'Well done as always. Congrats!', '2007-12-29 02:03:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342414, 623671, 64994, '<td valign="top">AWESOME!! My vote for the blue, congrats!!</td>', 'AWESOME!! My vote for the blue, congrats!!', '2007-12-29 02:24:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342418, 623227, 64994, '<td valign="top">Fantastic shot! thanks for the processing tips!! Congrats!!!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by atupdate:</b></div><hr/><i> Thanks everyone for kind words and the votes.  It figures, the one time I forget to put my processing steps in the comment section and I ribbon.  Here are the steps I used.<br/> <br/>1. Convert from raw using Raw Shooters Essentials<br/>Exposure Comp [+1.23]<br/>Highlight Contrast [22]<br/> <br/>2. Post process with Paint Shop Pro X<br/>One step noise reduction<br/>Clarify [+20]<br/>USM [radius 50 - strength 15 - clip 3]<br/>USM [radius 0.3 - strength 300 - clip 3]<br/>Levels [input 0-.94-255 / output 0-241]<br/>Curve - slight S curve to set black point<br/>Resize<br/>USM [radius 50 - strength 15 - clip 3]<br/>USM [radius 0.3 - strength 300 - clip 3]<br/> <br/>The HDR effect came from the very strong clarify action.  On most images, using clarify over a strength of 7 or 8 will provide nasty over processing artifacts.  The max setting of 20 seemed to work well for this image.<br/> <br/>Tim </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Fantastic shot! thanks for the processing tips!! Congrats!!! Originally posted by atupdate: Thanks everyone for kind words and the votes.  It figures, the one time I forget to put my processing steps in the comment section and I ribbon.  Here are the steps I used. 1. Convert from raw using Raw Shooters EssentialsExposure Comp [+1.23]Highlight Contrast [22] 2. Post process with Paint Shop Pro XOne step noise reductionClarify [+20]USM [radius 50 - strength 15 - clip 3]USM [radius 0.3 - strength 300 - clip 3]Levels [input 0-.94-255 / output 0-241]Curve - slight S curve to set black pointResizeUSM [radius 50 - strength 15 - clip 3]USM [radius 0.3 - strength 300 - clip 3] The HDR effect came from the very strong clarify action.  On most images, using clarify over a strength of 7 or 8 will provide nasty over processing artifacts.  The max setting of 20 seemed to work well for this image. Tim ', '2007-12-29 02:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342775, 623516, 40797, '<td valign="top">Amazing Deb!! I absolutely love this!! A true beauty!!Congratulations on your strong finish.</td>', 'Amazing Deb!! I absolutely love this!! A true beauty!!Congratulations on your strong finish.', '2007-12-29 10:08:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342880, 623671, 67697, '<td valign="top">Very nice wabi sabi. I like the imperfect (or incomplete) circle.  Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'Very nice wabi sabi. I like the imperfect (or incomplete) circle.  Congrats on the ribbon!', '2007-12-29 11:25:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342914, 623227, 64568, '<td valign="top">beautiful shot, well deserved ribbon ;-)</td>', 'beautiful shot, well deserved ribbon ;-)', '2007-12-29 11:56:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342944, 623433, 63398, '<td valign="top">I really like this! You got hammered pretty hard for what seems like a fine entry to me.</td>', 'I really like this! You got hammered pretty hard for what seems like a fine entry to me.', '2007-12-29 12:08:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342949, 622726, 63398, '<td valign="top">Okay.....this image is clean and decent, but it doesn''t really grab you and make you want anything from it like more of a description, or the pin itself; the back ground is a little flat, and it''s just kind of too ordinary. Maybe had it been brighter, or on a brighter background.....</td>', 'Okay.....this image is clean and decent, but it doesn''t really grab you and make you want anything from it like more of a description, or the pin itself; the back ground is a little flat, and it''s just kind of too ordinary. Maybe had it been brighter, or on a brighter background.....', '2007-12-29 12:12:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4342958, 623671, 69388, '<td valign="top">This is so simple and so, so beautiful!</td>', 'This is so simple and so, so beautiful!', '2007-12-29 12:20:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4343156, 622776, 66201, '<td valign="top">Ah - beautiful. I have taken many shots from this exact spot.... ancestral roots draw me back here. Nice idea to flip it. Well done.</td>', 'Ah - beautiful. I have taken many shots from this exact spot.... ancestral roots draw me back here. Nice idea to flip it. Well done.', '2007-12-29 14:30:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4343707, 622726, 82749, '<td valign="top">The pin is perhaps too ordinary (I think the key to this challenge was to take something at the exciting end of ordinary).  But apart from that, there are some things you could have done to make it more interesting:<br/>a) more interesting background (eg. place is on a wool sweater which has a pronounced texture, or on a blanket that looks like it could be of Hopi origin; or place it at an angle on a mirror so you can see both top and bottom of the pin)<br/>b) change the composition so that it is not right in the middle (consider the rule of thirds, for example)<br/>c) add other items to the image that either complement or contrast with the pin<br/> <br/>I also agree with the previous comments about glare/lighting<br/> <br/>Hope this helps.<br/></td>', 'The pin is perhaps too ordinary (I think the key to this challenge was to take something at the exciting end of ordinary).  But apart from that, there are some things you could have done to make it more interesting:a) more interesting background (eg. place is on a wool sweater which has a pronounced texture, or on a blanket that looks like it could be of Hopi origin; or place it at an angle on a mirror so you can see both top and bottom of the pin)b) change the composition so that it is not right in the middle (consider the rule of thirds, for example)c) add other items to the image that either complement or contrast with the pin I also agree with the previous comments about glare/lighting Hope this helps.', '2007-12-29 19:38:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4343754, 622726, 79955, '<td valign="top">Shannon,<br/>As the rest have mentioned quite accurately , the lighting can be improved further. You top lighted the image and caused<br/>very harsh shadows. Try to diffuse your lighting. If you used flash , use a diffuser (if you don''t have one just cover the flash head with<br/>tissue paper - use 1pc. to start with).<br/> <br/>By the way I did PM you hope it helps.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Shannon,As the rest have mentioned quite accurately , the lighting can be improved further. You top lighted the image and causedvery harsh shadows. Try to diffuse your lighting. If you used flash , use a diffuser (if you don''t have one just cover the flash head withtissue paper - use 1pc. to start with). By the way I did PM you hope it helps. ', '2007-12-29 19:57:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4344892, 623844, 65319, '<td valign="top">Deb...Congrats on this beautiful addition to your front page!!!</td>', 'Deb...Congrats on this beautiful addition to your front page!!!', '2007-12-30 12:19:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4345110, 622426, 30861, '<td valign="top">Speaking for myself (and I scored this one high already) you''d have gotten a full point more from me if you''d entered the less-processed version, which I think is utterly lovely. Great shot.</td>', 'Speaking for myself (and I scored this one high already) you''d have gotten a full point more from me if you''d entered the less-processed version, which I think is utterly lovely. Great shot.', '2007-12-30 14:34:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4345310, 623671, 9114, '<td valign="top">Techo, you do amazing work and I try to learn by watching you. I just totally do not get why this image works for so many people. To me it''s just a leaf in a bowl. I saw the B*W version of the CTF challenge and they love it there too.I just don''t get it. Please don''t take my comment as disrespect, I''m just trying to figure it out.<br/>Debbi</td>', 'Techo, you do amazing work and I try to learn by watching you. I just totally do not get why this image works for so many people. To me it''s just a leaf in a bowl. I saw the B*W version of the CTF challenge and they love it there too.I just don''t get it. Please don''t take my comment as disrespect, I''m just trying to figure it out.Debbi', '2007-12-30 16:13:14.000000', NULL, 0),
